---
/**
 * /design, the frame and the devices: the stamp, the mat, the touch rules, the
 * tablet rule (read live off this screen) and the share card.
 */
---

<section>
  <h2 class="sheet__head mono">Frame</h2>
  <p>
    Every page is a stamp on a cutting mat. The perforation is a mask cut out of
    the mat, so the mat shows through every hole. The edge is four strips that
    catch pointers, never one window-sized layer with a hole in it: Safari routes
    a scroll by a layer's box and ignores its clip.
  </p>
  <p>
    The mat and the stamp are <span class="code">100dvh</span> tall, so they
    follow the window when iPad Safari's toolbar collapses. On a touch screen the
    canvas behind them is paper and the paper's lift is dropped, because a fast
    fling paints unfinished tiles in the canvas colour.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under 1100px, or on any touch screen, there's no slide-over: a row on /tools
    or /sites opens the entry's own page. This screen, right now:
  </p>
  <dl class="spec" data-device>
    <div class="spec__row">
      <dt class="mono spec__label">Pointer</dt>
      <dd data-device-pointer>fine</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="spec__row">
      <dt class="mono spec__label">Slide-over</dt>
      <dd data-device-panel>on</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="spec__row">
      <dt class="mono spec__label">Window height</dt>
      <dd class="tabular-nums" data-device-height>--</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <p>
    A shared link shows the stamp too: the domain in an ink pill, the section in
    a chip of its mat's colour, the title, and a picture when there is one. Sized
    to read on a 300px message card.
  </p>
  <img class="card outlined" src="/og/tools.jpg" alt="The share card for /tools" width="1200" height="630" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
</section>

<script>
  import { PANEL_OFF } from "../../lib/detail-panel";

  const set = (key: string, text: string) => {
    const slot = document.querySelector(`[data-device-${key}]`);
    if (slot) slot.textContent = text;
  };
  const read = () => {
    set("pointer", matchMedia("(pointer: coarse)").matches ? "coarse (touch)" : "fine");
    set("panel", matchMedia(PANEL_OFF).matches ? "off, rows open the page" : "on");
    set("height", `${innerHeight}px`);
  };
  read();
  addEventListener("resize", read);
</script>

<style>
  .card {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
